  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1238 PM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nSatellite imagery shows East Idaho under ridge axis with weak\nshortwave departing to the east and strong closed low in the\nnorth Pacific. Most of East Idaho is clear but pockets of low\nclouds still linger in the northwest stretches of the Arco\nDesert towards the Divide. A series of shortwave features eject\ninland Sunday and again Monday night/Tuesday. The latter \nfeature may have the best chance at producing a few light \nshowers across northern zones, along with a drop of a few \ndegrees in daytime highs by Tuesday. Otherwise high pressure \nremains in control with temperatures remaining above normal for \nmuch of the week. Looking ahead to the potential pattern chance \nlate in the week or next weekend, deterministic models have \ntrended toward development of a deep split flow pattern late in \nthe week, delaying inland push of the northern stream trough. \nPrecipitation now looks to hold off until Friday night or \nSaturday, though a few ensemble members introduce precipitation \nas early as Friday afternoon.",
